# ── WhatsApp ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The gateway is int.chatway.in and the username is already set. PASTE THE
# TOKEN on the WHATSAPP_TOKEN line below and WhatsApp starts working — booking
# confirmations, check-in, bills, pickups, the lot.
#
# It is deliberately left empty here rather than committed: a token written
# into a file is a token in every backup and every copy of this project anybody
# is ever sent.
#
# AFTER EDITING THIS FILE, RUN ONCE:  php artisan config:clear
# Laravel caches this file. Until that command is run the old values are still
# what the application sees, which is why a token that "has been filled in"
# can still send nothing.
#
# To check what the running application actually has, without guessing:
#     php artisan whatsapp:test
# and to send one real message and see the gateway's own reply:
#     php artisan whatsapp:test 9876543210
# The same table is on the screen at Administration -> Notification Settings.
#
# WHATSAPP_DRIVER=log turns sending off on purpose: messages are written to
# storage/logs/laravel.log instead. Anything else with its keys missing is
# treated as a fault and says so, rather than quietly logging and looking like
# it worked.
